# Project key
#
# A short identifier (3-5 uppercase letters) for this project.
#
# What it is: a compact label for the project, like the "project key" in
# Jira (e.g. PROJ-123) or the "team key" / identifier in Linear (e.g. ENG-42).
# Other tools call it a prefix or a short code.
#
# How it is used: agents read this file to work out which project a session
# belongs to. For example, a session that implements ticket 6 here gets named
# "SPLT-6: Amazon Item Splits", so it is easy to spot in a list of sessions
# sorted by date instead of by project.
#
# Format: the first line that is not blank and does not start with "#" is the
# key. Keep it to one key.

SPLT
